  "name": "PLASMA RENIN ACTIVITY",
  "code": "1181",
  "cost": 0,
  "interpretation": "<ul>\n<li>PRA measures the activity of the plasma enzyme rennin, which plays a major role in the bodies regulation of blood&nbsp;pressure, thirst and urine output.</li>\n<li>Increase levels are seen in Addison&rsquo;s disease, liver cirrhosis, essential hypertention, hemorrhage, hypokalemia,malignant hypertention, rennin producing renal tumor, renovascular hypertention.</li>\n<li>Decrease levels are seen in vasopressin (ADH) therapy, salt retaining steroid therapy, salt sensitive essential<br>hypertention, primary hyperaldosteronism.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>LIMITATIONS:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Drugs that can affect rennin measurements are contraceptive pills, anti-hypertensives, diuretics, vasodilators.</li>\n<li>Sodium content of diet.</li>\n<li>Please correlate results with physiological variables such as time of collection, patient&rsquo;s posture, and either sodium&nbsp;intake of 24 hr urine sodium excretion.</li>\n</ul>\n<table style=\"border-collapse: collapse; width: 99.9716%;\" border=\"1\"><colgroup><col style=\"width: 66.078%;\"><col style=\"width: 14.0956%;\"><col style=\"width: 19.7978%;\"></colgroup>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td>Clinical condition&nbsp;</td>\n<td>Plasma rennin<br>activity&nbsp;</td>\n<td>Aldosterone</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Primary hyperaldosteronism</td>\n<td>Decreased</td>\n<td>Increased</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Malignant hypertension, renovascular hypertension</td>\n<td>Increased</td>\n<td>Increased</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Cushing syndrome, licorice ingestion, exogenous mineralocorticoids, Liddle&rsquo;s syndrome,congenital adrenal hyperplasia</td>\n<td>Decreased</td>\n<td>Decreased</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Adrenal insufficiency (Addison&rsquo;s disease), late onset congenital adrenal hyperplasia, high&nbsp;sodium diet</td>\n<td>Increased</td>\n<td>Decreased</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>",
